<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Gaston Guitart.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    Hi, this is Gaston GG. I write about diffefent aspects of distributed data systems
    that I find interesting. Ingesting, storing, and performing calculations on 
    large volumes of data reliably. And I do my best to point out pitfalls to avoid.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    Outside of this, I read constantly, listen to music and try to write my own
    with a guitar, piano, and one of those popular DAWs.
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    In these Posts, I try to favor code and measurements over opinion. Where reasonable, the
    code behind a post lives in a public repo with proper instructions and tests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Feedback, corrections, and contributions are welcome. Open an issue or
    a PR on the relevant repo, reach out on <a href="https://github.com/ggasg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>, or email <a href="mailto:gaston.guitart@gmail.com">gaston.guitart@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Post text is free to reuse and adapt under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY 4.0</a>, citation back to me is the only condition. Code, here and in linked repos, is <a href="https://github.com/ggasg/ggasg.github.io/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MIT</a>.
  </p>
